{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Oil for lighting.</b> For the needs of the lighting, as is the rule. The sages of the generation said that the sense of \"and for the incense of spices\" is inverted, and so it is: \"the spices for the incense.\" If so, why was it not stated thus: \"and for the anointing oil, spices\"? Moreover: \"and the spice and the oil for lighting and for the anointing oil and for the incense of spices\" (below, 35:28). The correct view in my eyes is that the word \"spices\" includes the anointing oil and the spices that are mixed with the incense-spices. And thus is the tradition of truth:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved למטה לה כח to Exodus 35:28 by counting from the verse cited (25:6); the abbreviation לה likely stands for chapter 35."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:12.343182909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}